WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.620
Hey, welcome to Planetarian Daily, episode 90 for June 15, 2026.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.800
Here's your science and health briefing.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:11.520
Underground fungal networks span 110 quadrillion kilometers

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:16.140
and move 4 billion tons of carbon dioxide into soils each year.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.700
Researchers compiled data to estimate the total length

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:24.260
of mycorrhizal fungal filaments at 110 quadrillion kilometers.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.520
The networks move roughly 4 billion tons

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.620
of carbon dioxide into soils annually.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.020
They support plant growth and influence climate regulation

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:34.100
through carbon storage.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:37.080
The mapping provides a baseline for tracking

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.880
how these systems respond to environmental change.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.600
Most people picture soil as a mix of minerals, water,

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.220
and plant roots with only scattered microbes.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:51.200
In reality, mycorrhizal fungi form continuous living filaments

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.740
that link plants across entire landscapes.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.320
Right now, as you stand or sit,

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.220
these threads are exchanging nutrients and carbon

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.520
between roots that may be meters apart.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:08.380
One memorable scale is that the total length reaches 110 quadrillion kilometers worldwide.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.820
The networks move 4 billion tons of carbon dioxide into soils each year,

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.180
a flux comparable to major geological processes.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.560
Next time you walk across grass or forest floor,

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.760
remember the hidden connections beneath

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:26.340
are actively redistributing resources and storing carbon.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:30.120
Watch for field studies that measure how drought or warming

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.300
alters the density of these filaments in different ecosystems.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.040
Now, shifting to a very different area of research,

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.700
an international team produced the first full connectome

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.700
of all neuron connections in the central nervous system

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.000
of an adult fruit fly.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:49.360
The map covers both brain and ventral nerve cord regions,

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.040
multiple labs at Harvard Medical School

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:54.060
and Princeton University led the effort.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.100
This resource enables direct testing of how specific circuits control behavior.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:04.020
Neuroscientists can now trace how defined circuits produce specific behaviors

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.620
and test predictions by targeted manipulation.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:11.220
The resource also serves as a template for comparing wiring changes

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.640
across genetic or environmental conditions.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.340
On a different note,

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:18.780
drone tracking of wild honey bees showed each insect

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.120
maintains its own consistent path between foraging sites.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.360
Some roads repeated so exactly that bees

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:28.000
passed within centimeters of prior positions.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.500
Trees and other landmarks stabilize the paths

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.520
while open fields like corn increased variation.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:38.080
The findings highlight how insects use visual cues

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:40.160
for navigation in natural settings.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:44.040
Next up, plasma proteomic analysis

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.580
assessed biological age across more than 40 cell types.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:51.580
Accelerated aging in particular cell populations correlated

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.880
with higher risk for specific diseases.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:58.260
The signatures also identified individuals showing slower aging

00:02:58.260 --> 00:02:59.540
in certain cell types.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.560
This approach offers a way to measure heterogeneous aging rates

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:04.820
from a single blood sample.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:08.120
Researchers identified proteomic signatures

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.380
that reflect the biological age of individual cell types.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.100
These markers forecast a disease risk

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.220
and resilience across multiple conditions.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.300
The study linked distinct aging profiles

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:22.420
in different cell populations to later clinical events.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.900
Now, shifting to a very different area of research.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:30.320
A forward genetic screen in canner-habitatis elegans,

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:33.220
ATFs-1 mutants uncover genes

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:35.700
that limit dopaminergic neuron loss

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:38.140
from alpha-synucleon over expression.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:45.300
Loss of JmJD 1.2, JmJD 3.1, or TWK-14,

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:48.000
increased neutrogenaring in this background.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:54.440
The JmJD genes encode H3K-27 EME-3D methalases

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:59.300
while TWK-14 encodes a potassium channel ortholog.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:03.620
The results point to chromatin and membrane potential pathways

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:05.940
that normally buffer protein toxicity.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:07.780
On a different note,

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:10.440
a randomized crossover trial tested

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:12.440
gate phase synchronized stimulation

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.800
against continuous deep brain stimulation.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:18.140
The adaptive approach proved feasible and safe

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:19.540
while lowering fall rates.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:22.360
Neural decoding drew on principles

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:25.820
of locomotor encoding to adjust stimulation in real time.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.680
Participants showed improved gate control

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:29.960
during daily activities.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:33.280
Next up, a quantitative imaging system

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.800
captured cellular dynamics during EMT

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:38.480
in human-induced pleuropotent stem cells.

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:42.460
Progression differed between 2D and 3D culture formats

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:44.720
and tied to basement membrane integrity.

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:47.600
The platform integrates multiple readouts

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.860
to follow state transitions in real time.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:52.240
It supports systematic comparison

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:55.000
of EMT regulators across geometries.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:58.500
The system records changes in cell morphology

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:00.480
and marker expression simultaneously.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.480
Researchers use the platform to examine

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:06.460
how matrix properties influence transition timing.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.600
Data outputs include time-resolved maps

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:12.260
of protein localization during the process.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:16.200
Now, shifting to a very different area of research,

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:18.620
high-sea foundation was pre-trained

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:20.840
on a large collection of high-sea data sets

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:22.600
for 3D genome studies.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:24.720
The model supports single cell

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:27.480
and multi-omics applications across species.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:30.680
It captures chromatin architecture features

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.840
that generalize beyond the training data.

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:35.700
Researchers can apply it to new data sets

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:37.420
for epigenomic interpretation.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:41.020
Training included data sets from multiple organisms

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:42.740
to improve feature detection.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.280
The architecture allows fine-tuning

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.280
on user-provided high-sea maps

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.060
without retraining from scratch.

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:52.760
Output embeddings preserve both local contact patterns

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:56.140
and larger scale compartmentalization signals.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:57.880
On a different note,

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.660
climate models and field data show frost-driven rock breakdown

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:03.460
moving to higher elevations.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:07.080
Lower elevations experience fewer freeze-thaw cycles

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:08.260
as temperatures rise.

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:11.500
The redistribution alters where and when

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:13.080
rock falls are most likely.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:16.900
The study maps changing hazards from mountain landscapes.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.540
Projections indicate the zone of peak frost weathering

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:23.020
will shift up-slope by several hundred meters

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:24.040
in coming decades.

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:27.260
Field measurements in the Pyrenees confirmed

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:30.440
reduced fracture rates at previously active sites.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:34.340
Updated hazard maps incorporate both temperature trends

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:36.460
and rock-type susceptibility.

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:40.720
Next up, Australian researchers compare thermal tolerance

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:42.600
across bee-nesting strategies.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:45.780
Stem-nesting species showed greater vulnerability

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:48.060
to rising temperatures in the short term.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:52.280
Ground-nesting bees can shift depth to avoid extreme heat.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.560
The difference arises from the limited thermal buffering

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:56.460
in plant stems.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:58.280
On a different note,

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:02.000
Kelly's School of Business experiments found consistent elevation

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:05.340
of self-sacrificial acts in judgments of heroism.

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:08.700
Participants rated sacrificial actions higher

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:11.900
even when outcomes matched non-sacrificial alternatives.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:14.660
The pattern held across different scenarios

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:15.540
and demographics.

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:18.660
The work examines how observers weigh intent

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:19.700
versus result.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:23.180
Ratings remained stable when participants were asked

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:25.280
to justify their choices in writing.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:29.240
Similar elevation of sacrifice appeared in both student

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:30.880
and online adult samples.

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:33.680
The design varied outcome equivalents

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:35.840
to isolate the role of personal cost.

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:36.800
Next up,

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:40.440
researchers traced off flavors in concentrated way

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:41.560
to residual minerals.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.540
A new processing step removes these minerals

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:46.220
while preserving the smoother mouth

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:48.320
field from prior concentration methods.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:51.280
The approach targets the source of bitterness

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.680
without compromising functional properties.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:57.480
It aims to enhance consumer acceptance of protein beverages.

00:07:58.340 --> 00:07:59.900
Mineral removal was achieved

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:02.300
through selective ion exchange columns

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:04.140
calibrated for way streams.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:07.580
Sensory panels confirmed reduced bitterness scores

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:11.040
without changes in viscosity or solubility metrics.

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:14.060
The method maintains protein recovery rates

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:16.240
above those of untreated concentrates.

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:19.880
Now, shifting to a very different area of research.

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:22.820
Archaeologist examined a female skeleton

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:25.080
whose brain had been extracted after death.

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:28.500
The remaining bones were arranged deliberately for burial.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:31.100
Some bones had been shaped into tools.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:34.400
The find illustrates specific mortuary practices

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:35.180
in the period.

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:38.060
Next up, Taylor and Francis released

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:40.540
the initial plain language summary of publication

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:42.020
in a veterinary journal.

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:44.720
The format translates technical findings

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:47.460
into accessible language for broader audiences.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:49.900
It targets animal health practitioners

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:51.940
and interested non-specialists.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:55.080
The initiative extends open access practices

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:56.900
already used in human medicine.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:01.080
The summary accompanies a study on equine joint therapies

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:03.500
and includes definitions of key terms.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:07.080
Editors worked with authors to preserve accuracy

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:09.560
while shortening methods and results sections.

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:12.940
Future issues will include similar summaries

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:14.240
as a standard feature.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:18.320
New maps and models keep revealing how living systems scale

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:19.860
from cells to landscapes.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:24.020
Keep an eye on updates from the High C Foundation model work

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:26.200
on cross-species chromatin analysis.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:29.160
That covers today's science and health news.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:31.040
Share this with someone who's curious

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:32.180
about the latest research.

